test_pidxclean — PID_EXIT auxiliary-table cleanup self-test
============================================================

Phase 2 chunk 3 of the net-stack quality plan: when PM notifies
inet that a process has exited, inet must reclaim every slot the
process owned — not only its UDP/TCP sockets, but also the
auxiliary tables that hold an owner_tid:

- ICMP ping pending-reply table (`inet_ping_table`, 4 slots).
  `ping foo` registers a slot; if the peer never replies and the
  process exits without polling, the slot was leaking.
- ARP-pending UDP queue (`inet_pending_udp`, 2 slots).  A
  datagram parked while we wait for an ARP reply was being
  retransmitted on behalf of the dead process when the reply
  landed.

This test drives the inet self-test that exercises both paths
synthetically — no real socket, no real network. The inet side
parks one ping slot and one pending-UDP slot under a synthetic
owner_tid, runs the cleanup helpers, and verifies both slots
freed.

Prints `pidxclean: ok` on pass or `pidxclean: failed N` where
N is the failure-step code returned by the inet self-test
(0x10..0x1f = ping path, 0x20..0x2f = pending-UDP path).

    module oskit.bin.test_pidxclean

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.{pid_exit_cleanup_test}


    print_uhex(v: int)
        val hi = (v >> 4) & 0xf
        val lo = v & 0xf
        var b: [2]byte
        if hi < 10
            b[0] = byte('0' + hi)
        else
            b[0] = byte('a' + (hi - 10))
        if lo < 10
            b[1] = byte('0' + lo)
        else
            b[1] = byte('a' + (lo - 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 2))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("pidxclean: failed 0x")
        print_uhex(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val rc = pid_exit_cleanup_test()
        if rc != 0
            fail(rc)
            return
        puts("pidxclean: ok\n")
        exit()
